# There is no integer division — `7 / 2` is 3.5 and `//` is not an operator —
# so ወደታች is how a program divides and keeps a whole number (§8.7).
# expect: 3 4 3 2
# expect: 7 0
# expect: ["አበበ"፣ "ከበደ"]
# expect: ["ሀ"፣ ""፣ "ለ"]
# expect: ["ሰ"፣ "ላ"፣ "ም"]
# expect: አበበ ከበደ
# expect: 1-2-3
# expect: [ሰላም]
ጻፍ(ወደታች(7 / 2)፣ ወደላይ(7 / 2)፣ አቅርብ(2.5)፣ አቅርብ(2.4))
ጻፍ(ፍጹም(0 - 7)፣ ፍጹም(0))

# One argument splits on runs of whitespace and drops the empties.
ጻፍ(ከፋፍል("  አበበ   ከበደ  "))

# A named separator keeps them: a program counting fields wants to know.
ጻፍ(ከፋፍል("ሀ,,ለ"፣ ","))

# An empty separator gives the code points, as ርዝመት counts them (§4.3).
ጻፍ(ከፋፍል("ሰላም"፣ ""))

ጻፍ(አገናኝ(["አበበ"፣ "ከበደ"]))
ጻፍ(አገናኝ([1፣ 2፣ 3]፣ "-"))
ጻፍ("[" + ከርክም("   ሰላም   ") + "]")
